00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.370
Today, I got inspired by Victor Cheng,

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.250
and if you don't know him, check him out.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.190
He has a website, caseinterview.com,
where he helps people

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:59.040
to master the consulting case
interviews, great resource,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.190
check it out, caseinterview.com,

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.300
and I received a newsletter
from him where he talked about

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.300
the topic Problem Talker
Versus Problem Solver.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.270
He contrasts two type of people;

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.360
those who talk about problems
and those who actually

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.980
solve problems, and this was
a topic that resonated with me

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.540
a lot because I observed these two

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.250
different types of mentality
a lot in the last years.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.210
I've seen these type of
people, and when I read this,

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:31.310
I completely agreed that
this is what is going on

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:33.340
and that these are the two types of people

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:36.610
that are out there, and trust
me, one of these two types

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.880
is clearly better than the
other, and I'd like to help you

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.910
understand the differences,
and also give you some tips

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:46.470
how you can rather become a problem solver

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.710
than just a problem talker,
what the differences are,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.250
and why this is so important,
why all organizations

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.110
need lots and lots of problem solvers,

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.970
but problem talkers aren't
really what is interesting

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.820
and necessary and helpful to the people.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.330
So, what are problem talkers,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.420
to start with this group of people?

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:09.020
Problem talkers like
to talk about problems.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.110
They like to identify problems,

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.550
to see them, and to describe them.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.770
So, Victor Cheng here gives three examples

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.090
of what problem talkers do.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.660
Let's just go over some of them.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.817
So it's, for instance, somebody who says,

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:26.197
"Boss, this budgeting process
is just so inefficient,

00:02:26.197 --> 00:02:28.487
"there's no use of it,
and it's just wasting

00:02:28.487 --> 00:02:30.920
"everybody's time," right, this would be

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.070
a typical statement of a problem talker.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:36.357
Or, "Hey, the way that we
orient on new employees,

00:02:36.357 --> 00:02:39.417
"the way that we onboard
them, just doesn't work,

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:41.207
"it's not efficient and not working

00:02:41.207 --> 00:02:44.290
"for these new colleagues," or
Is driving throughout a city

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.737
and you say, "Hey, this
tree is just hanging

00:02:46.737 --> 00:02:50.217
"in front of the stop sign,
this is so unprofessional.

00:02:50.217 --> 00:02:52.287
"Somebody needs to do something about it.

00:02:52.287 --> 00:02:55.637
"Somebody needs to inform the
city, this needs to change

00:02:55.637 --> 00:02:58.010
"because it's just unsafe," right?

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:01.330
So, these are typical things
that problem talkers will do,

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.260
and it's just really
important to understand

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.670
the psychology behind all that.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.010
Why would people behave in this way?

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.590
Well, and I think an important
and the key part of that

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:15.900
is that it's because it makes
these people feel intelligent,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.127
feel smart, "Hey, I'm the
one who identified this,

00:03:19.127 --> 00:03:22.297
"I got this, obviously
everybody else cannot see this

00:03:22.297 --> 00:03:23.967
"because the problem
was still there, right,

00:03:23.967 --> 00:03:26.737
"but I'm the one who got
this, I identified it,

00:03:26.737 --> 00:03:29.567
"and if everybody would
be as smart as I am,

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:31.710
"then things like that would not happen."

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.530
I think this is a characteristic
of such a problem talker

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.200
that the way that he
sees the problems is that

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.620
these problems are always
caused by the other people.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.740
The other people are
responsible for these problems,

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.560
but it's never the problem
solver, and if only

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.180
these other people would
do their jobs right,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.480
the problems like that
wouldn't exist, right?

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.810
If only the other people
would take their job

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.590
as seriously as the problem talker does,

00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.760
then the world would
be a much better place.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:03.800
So, let's now contrast that
with how a problem solver

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.440
would approach these types of situations,

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.990
and as the name says, the problem solver

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:12.310
does not only talk about all
the things that need to change,

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:15.480
but he actually tries to make a difference

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.210
and to make an impact,
and to actually change

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.880
and solve these problems,
and yes, it is true

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.940
that very often it is just
not possible that you,

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.580
as one person, organization,
can solve all the problems

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.330
by yourself, even though I
would say the people frequently

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:35.750
underestimate the impact
that they actually can have

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.690
if they really, really
wanted to make a difference.

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.440
But yes, it is true that
this is not possible,

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.550
but then what the problem solver does is,

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.990
at least he does not only
try to come up, at least,

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.000
with an idea or a suggestion
how it could work,

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.950
but he also tries to go the
first steps in that direction

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.030
to not only come up with, yeah obviously,

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:57.300
this is what would need
to happen, but also

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.640
to go in the first steps in that direction

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.890
to actually make that a reality.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:04.160
And, let's now go over these examples

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.890
that we just discussed a bit earlier

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.500
about how a problem solver
talks about the problems.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.750
Let's go over these examples,
what the problem solver

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:14.040
now actually could do,
and now starting with

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:17.000
the budgeting process,
the problem solver would

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.400
not only say that the
budgeting process doesn't work,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.190
but he would make a couple of suggestions

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.240
of how the budget process
could actually improve,

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.420
and what substantiate these suggestions,

00:05:28.420 --> 00:05:30.740
maybe talk to some colleagues to make sure

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.570
that this really makes sense, and then,

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:36.410
you wouldn't stop here,
but he then would reach out

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:40.140
to the person who actually
is responsible for shaping

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.190
the budgeting process, and
then just proposes to him,

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:46.390
just in an open and
constructive way, raises topic

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.240
and just make a few ideas
how this could change,

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.220
and if you do not do that
in a confrontive way,

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.430
very frequently you will
see that people actually

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:57.430
quite responsible for good
ideas because these good ideas

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:00.470
then hopefully make the
work and the life easier

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.330
for everybody who was involved, right,

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:04.860
so why wouldn't then
the person responsible

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.730
for the budgeting process
not take on that idea?

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:10.640
So, he goes that step in that direction.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.850
The other example was
the onboarding process

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:16.270
for new employees that
apparently just did not work,

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:18.280
so what would a problem solver do?

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.740
He would not only complain
about the onboarding process

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.950
that wouldn't work,
but he would just start

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.450
creating a few documents,
maybe a checklist

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:29.110
that new employees can use.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.540
And that order for them
that the onboarding process

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.410
would be a bit more
smoothly and more helpful,

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.130
so some resources, for
instance, that he would've

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.220
found helpful when he joined the company,

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:42.200
and then once he gives this
to a couple of colleagues

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.900
in his direct team that maybe
then you'll join us then.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.710
If this picks up and people
see that this is helpful,

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.950
very likely has an awesome opportunity

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.460
to push this to the larger
department, or maybe even

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.490
the whole organization because
he just made an impact there,

00:06:56.490 --> 00:06:58.500
and this will show an
initiative, and this is how

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.820
he really can solve these problems.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.650
Or, the third example was
the example with the tree

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.940
that is hanging in front of the stop sign,

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.530
where the problem solver
now could just call the city

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.000
and let them know that
this problem exists,

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:15.300
let them know where exactly
the street is located,

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:17.740
where exactly it is
covering the stop sign,

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.660
and pretty likely then the city,

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.920
once it has been officially informed,

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.100
it will do something
about it, and make sure

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.370
that this tree then gets
taken away from the stop sign,

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.550
and now the safety is restored again.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.270
So, these are things that
problem solvers would do.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:35.490
They try to solve the
problem, and they do not only

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:38.520
talk about the problems,
and from my experience,

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.930
problem solvers like
that belong to the most

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:45.910
valuable people that
organizations can have.

00:07:45.910 --> 00:07:49.460
Organizations can never
have enough problem solvers,

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:52.740
but pretty much do not
need problem talkers

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.590
because the reality is that,
even though the problem talker

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.480
maybe believes that he is so smart

00:07:57.480 --> 00:08:01.130
because he sees the
problem, pretty usually,

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:04.280
these problems are perceived
by many, many people,

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:07.310
but the reality is that
most of these people

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:08.630
don't do anything about them.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:13.230
Most people are problem talkers,
but only very few people

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:16.300
are problem solvers, that's
just the truth, guys.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.380
In fact, this is just natural.

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.850
This is how we humans behave.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.610
We tend to believe that
if there's a problem,

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.220
it's not because of us, but
it's because of other people

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:28.130
who made the mistake, and it's something

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:30.810
that I sometimes catch myself as well.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.750
If I watch myself, I see that I have

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.720
such a thought that there's a problem,

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.020
and probably somebody else
is responsible for that,

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:41.350
but if I'm really honest to
myself, I know and I understand

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.010
that I would have the
power to do something

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:47.760
about that as well, and this
would be now my advice to you.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.900
Whenever you have such
a thought in your head,

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.440
this is going bad, this doesn't work,

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.850
these idiots from the other department,

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.720
why aren't they doing a better job?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.890
Always ask what can you do,
what do you have in your power

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.710
to actually make a difference
and to make an impact

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:08.030
for your organization, because
if you adopt that mindset,

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.750
you will not only be a problem talker,

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.777
but you will be a problem solver,

00:09:12.777 --> 00:09:15.480
and this is what organizations will value,

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.890
and this is how you will be successful

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:20.960
in the end as an employee and as a person

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.560
in your whole life, I would say.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.830
So, thank you for watching.

